-- title:
--   Constant field extension from ℚ̄ to ℂ with base change of places
-- statement:
--   Let $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denote `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-algebra structure which is a curve over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ in the project's sense, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ with $D(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at each place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$, each place has residue field finite as a $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-module, and $\Omega_{F/\bar{\mathbb Q}}$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$; assume moreover $F$ is essentially of finite type over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. Let $\iota : \bar{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism. The conclusion provides a field $F_{\mathbb C}$ with a $\mathbb C$-algebra structure, which is again a curve over $\mathbb C$ in the same sense and essentially of finite type over $\mathbb C$, together with a ring homomorphism $t : F \to F_{\mathbb C}$ and a map $P \mapsto P_{\mathbb C}$ from places of $F/\bar{\mathbb Q}$ to places of $F_{\mathbb C}/\mathbb C$ (a place being a valuation subring, distinct from the whole field, containing the image of the base field and a principal ideal ring), such that: $t$ restricted to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ agrees with $\iota$ followed by the structure map of $F_{\mathbb C}$; the subfield of $F_{\mathbb C}$ generated by the images of $\mathbb C$ and of $t$ is all of $F_{\mathbb C}$; every finite subset of $F$ that is linearly independent over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ has $t$-image linearly independent over $\mathbb C$ (only finite subsets are asserted, not arbitrary families); for every place $P$ of $F/\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every $x \in F$, one has $t(x) \in P_{\mathbb C}$ if and only if $x \in P$; and $P \mapsto P_{\mathbb C}$ is injective.
--
--   This is the constant field extension of a one-variable function field along an embedding of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ into $\mathbb C$, packaged with the three comparison clauses (generation, linear disjointness on finite sets, and compatibility of valuation subrings) needed to transfer divisor and place data across the base change. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld component of the development, in the passage from a Hecke curve over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ to its complex uniformisation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_constantFieldExtension_place_of_isAlgClosed.lean

